<h2 class="no-num" id="conformance">Conformance</h2>

The key words "MUST", "MUST NOT", "SHOULD" and "MAY" in this document are to be interpreted as described in BCP 14 [[!RFC2119]] [[!RFC8174]] when, and only when, they appear in all capitals.

Everything in this specification is normative, except the sections marked as informative, the examples, the notes and the issues.

This specification defines four conformance classes:

: <dfn export>Conforming metadata document</dfn>
:: An RDF document that describes at least one `tss:Snippet` and meets every requirement in this specification on a metadata document, a snippet, a field, embedded points and a stored summary. For an external snippet, this includes the requirements on the properties that describe the data file, its [=Time Grid=] and its value encoding, but not on the contents of the data file.
: <dfn export>Conforming data</dfn>
:: The points of a snippet, embedded or in its data file, that meet the requirements on points: the time of every point (on a [=Time Grid=], its step), the key, the lexical form of the values, and the [=Time Window=]. The points of an embedded snippet are part of its metadata document; the rows of a data file are not.
: <dfn export>Conforming consumer</dfn>
:: Software that reads a conforming metadata document and its data as this specification says: it selects the rules by `tss:embedded`, reads the points as [[#points]] or [[#data-files]] says, reads the times as [[#times]] says, decodes the values of a field with a value encoding ([[#value-encoding]]), applies the [=Time Window=] and the [=Empty Value=] rules, and reports an error where this specification calls something an error. A <dfn export>conforming expander</dfn> is a conforming consumer that also expands a snippet into observations as [[#expanding]] says.
: <dfn export>Conforming writer</dfn>
:: Software that changes the points of an [=Embedded Snippet=] only by the [=Write=] of [[#updating]], and that leaves a conforming metadata document conforming after every Write.
